Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.98,0:00:19.38,Default,,0,0,0,,The following tale begins on\NJune 5th in the year 1972.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.54,0:00:24.94,Default,,0,0,0,,It was a dark and humid night in\NAmerica's deep south when the first
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.02,0:00:29.14,Default,,0,0,0,,cry of a newborn child rang through\Nthe halls of a maternity hospital.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.60,0:00:31.43,Default,,0,0,0,,However,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.51,0:00:34.27,Default,,0,0,0,,before that baby had the\Nchance to see the light of day,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.36,0:00:36.01,Default,,0,0,0,,his life expired while still
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.82,0:00:38.22,Default,,0,0,0,,curled in the arms of his mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.30,0:00:39.48,Default,,0,0,0,,To the young mother,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.64,0:00:42.06,Default,,0,0,0,,who had never once felt that\Nshe had been living a life
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.14,0:00:45.08,Default,,0,0,0,,that consisted of any\Nhappiness or sense of purpose,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.16,0:00:46.48,Default,,0,0,0,,her newborn son
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.12,0:00:50.60,Default,,0,0,0,,was going to be a symbol of the hope\Nthat she would have a better future.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.68,0:00:52.72,Default,,0,0,0,,With her first child lost to her,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.94,0:00:55.86,Default,,0,0,0,,that potential happiness she\Nlonged for was lost as well,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.94,0:00:57.88,Default,,0,0,0,,and she was unable to accept
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.94,0:00:59.77,Default,,0,0,0,,his death.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.85,0:01:03.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Before the doctors and nurses could\Nlearn of the baby's unfortunate passing,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.62,0:01:08.18,Default,,0,0,0,,the young mother slipped out of her bed\Nas if she were a phantom in the night.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.26,0:01:10.68,Default,,0,0,0,,She made her way into\Nanother room where she
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.76,0:01:13.35,Default,,0,0,0,,replaced her deceased\Nchild with one who was
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.96,0:01:16.52,Default,,0,0,0,,born the same day and made him her own.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.60,0:01:19.44,Default,,0,0,0,,This other baby which\Nshe took was one of a set
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.06,0:01:21.06,Default,,0,0,0,,of fraternal twins.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.14,0:01:24.85,Default,,0,0,0,,To this day, the incident was\Nnever questioned or investigated,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.10,0:01:27.82,Default,,0,0,0,,and not Even a single\Nsoul suspected a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.86,0:01:33.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Mama, whose grave is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.14,0:01:36.26,Default,,0,0,0,,They were born the same day as me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.02,0:01:38.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Died then, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.44,0:01:40.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Enrico. Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.36,0:01:44.94,Default,,0,0,0,,The truth of the matter is,\Nyou had a younger brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.40,0:01:48.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The two of you were fraternal twins. Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.54,0:01:52.01,Default,,0,0,0,,But he passed away at the\Nhospital right after he was born.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.58,0:01:54.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Pray for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.80,0:02:00.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Afterwards, we decided to\Ngive him the name Dominic.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.18,0:02:08.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Lord, answer my plea.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.84,0:02:12.84,Default,,0,0,0,,My brother and I were born on the\Nsame day, but I lived and he died.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.20,0:02:17.42,Default,,0,0,0,,For what reason did fate choose to\Ntake my brother's life and not mine?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.24,0:02:22.18,Default,,0,0,0,,And why do humans experience\Nhappiness and misfortune?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.98,0:02:24.70,Default,,0,0,0,,What is true happiness?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.80,0:02:28.66,Default,,0,0,0,,At this time, Enrico was age 15.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.84,0:02:32.84,Default,,0,0,0,,His great-grandmother on his father's\Nside was an Italian immigrant.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.26,0:02:37.06,Default,,0,0,0,,He is descended from a prestigious\Nand influential family in Venice,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.14,0:02:38.80,Default,,0,0,0,,in which one of his family members became
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.88,0:02:42.18,Default,,0,0,0,,a famous clergyman during\Nthe 18th century. So,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.48,0:02:45.64,Default,,0,0,0,,when young Enrico declared he\Nwanted to attend a seminary,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.72,0:02:48.72,Default,,0,0,0,,there wasn't one member of\Nhis family who objected.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.74,0:02:56.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, is someone here? Who's there?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.30,0:03:00.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me, what are you doing in here?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.42,0:03:02.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold it!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.48,0:03:03.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this book yours?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.04,0:03:08.02,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a famous biography\Nabout a clergyman who.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.10,0:03:11.04,Default,,0,0,0,,commits adultery and runs\Noff to become a painter.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.52,0:03:15.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Would a believer in God ever\Nread such a scandalous scripture?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.70,0:03:16.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Sergius, who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.00,0:03:18.62,Default,,0,0,0,,How did you get in this place?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.70,0:03:19.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Except for on Sundays,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.96,0:03:24.25,Default,,0,0,0,,this charnel house does not allow\Nmembers of the general public to enter.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.02,0:03:29.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I am aware of the restrictions, but\NI am deathly allergic to the sun.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.52,0:03:32.82,Default,,0,0,0,,If I am not mistaken, the\Nsun sets at 6.19 today.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.34,0:03:37.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Until that time comes, I cannot go\Nhome, which is why I rested in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.14,0:03:40.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.42,0:03:44.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, in that case, is there\Nanything I can do to help you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.88,0:03:45.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.48,0:03:48.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.39,0:03:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,That's unfortunate.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.84,0:03:51.67,Default,,0,0,0,,it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.75,0:03:53.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't tell the head priest\Nabout encountering you,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.56,0:03:55.85,Default,,0,0,0,,but you must be gone when the sun sets.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.10,0:03:59.93,Default,,0,0,0,,My, my.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.16,0:04:01.69,Default,,0,0,0,,You're an interesting one.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.36,0:04:04.19,Default,,0,0,0,,How so?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.40,0:04:06.26,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not going to throw me out.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.34,0:04:10.05,Default,,0,0,0,,What if I were a burglar who came\Nhere to rob this place of its
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.44,0:04:13.12,Default,,0,0,0,,most valuable artwork,\Nor worse, to kill you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.20,0:04:15.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Or perhaps you're just saying I can stay,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.68,0:04:18.32,Default,,0,0,0,,but you actually plan to\Nrat me out to the police.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.40,0:04:20.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that what you want me to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.20,0:04:25.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Though a thief wouldn't lie about a\Nsun allergy, it doesn't seem plausible.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.58,0:04:28.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Not even the devil would\Ntell such a blatant lie.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.10,0:04:30.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on a moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.56,0:04:34.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you just twist your ankle\Nbecause of me? Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.62,0:04:35.74,Default,,0,0,0,,No, it isn't that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.12,0:04:37.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Please don't worry about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.46,0:04:39.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been like this since my birth.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.50,0:04:42.62,Default,,0,0,0,,They say I was born with\Ntwisted toes on my left foot.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.70,0:04:45.41,Default,,0,0,0,,However, it doesn't\Nhinder my ability to walk.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.52,0:04:51.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you believe in gravity\Nbetween individuals?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.72,0:04:54.22,Default,,0,0,0,,You ended up tripping\Nover me, of all people.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.30,0:04:56.48,Default,,0,0,0,,But did you know it was for a reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.18,0:04:59.36,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.66,0:05:05.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Take this arrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.16,0:05:08.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Consider it a thank you present.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.36,0:05:12.48,Default,,0,0,0,,If you do not wish to accept it,\Nthat is still perfectly fine with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.86,0:05:16.33,Default,,0,0,0,,But are not all meetings of\Nfate their own form of gravity?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.52,0:05:21.34,Default,,0,0,0,,We only did just meet, so I don't know\Nwhat your first impression of me is.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.52,0:05:25.11,Default,,0,0,0,,But I am a traveler fueled by\Nthe hope of fateful encounters.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.30,0:05:28.12,Default,,0,0,0,,If ever you feel like\Nseeing me again someday,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.60,0:05:31.64,Default,,0,0,0,,aim that desire towards\Nthe arrow and pray.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.18,0:05:35.30,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter how many years\Nmight have passed since now.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.62,0:05:36.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Got it?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.82,0:05:39.44,Default,,0,0,0,,All I ask is for you to keep that in mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.98,0:05:44.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Once we reach sundown, it\Nshall be like I was never here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.84,0:05:55.68,Default,,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.72,0:05:57.64,Default,,0,0,0,,My toes!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.96,0:05:59.43,Default,,0,0,0,,The toes on my left foot!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.18,0:06:01.36,Default,,0,0,0,,They're not twisted!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.42,0:06:03.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.42,0:06:04.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Who even are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.84,0:06:12.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, father
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.74,0:06:16.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen to my plea
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.66,0:06:19.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I beg of you I have a confession to make
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.64,0:06:24.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes well One moment I'll get the\Npriest I'm stricken with disease
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.34,0:06:27.20,Default,,0,0,0,,And I fear I'm going to die
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.74,0:06:30.86,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no cure That can help me now
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.48,0:06:35.34,Default,,0,0,0,,But My illness isn't what\NI'm here To confess about
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.56,0:06:38.88,Default,,0,0,0,,My sin Was to my family
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.68,0:06:43.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Sixteen years ago, on\Nthe night of June 5th,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.60,0:06:48.31,Default,,0,0,0,,after my newborn baby drew his first and\Nfinal breath, I traded him for another.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.12,0:06:54.10,Default,,0,0,0,,While no one was looking, I took a\Nstranger's baby and left mine in his place.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.86,0:06:56.48,Default,,0,0,0,,That baby was a twin.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.58,0:07:02.36,Default,,0,0,0,,When I think about the baby's\Nparents, I am overcome with guilt.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.96,0:07:08.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Though he wasn't mine, I raised the\Nchild to the best of my ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.06,0:07:10.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I was so happy,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.88,0:07:15.65,Default,,0,0,0,,and the little boy I watched go through\Nlife grew up to be such a fine young man.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.16,0:07:16.99,Default,,0,0,0,,However,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.07,0:07:22.24,Default,,0,0,0,,if I die without ever confessing, what\Nwould happen if I told him the truth,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.46,0:07:24.34,Default,,0,0,0,,that he has a brother somewhere?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.64,0:07:26.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Though if he finally learns what happened,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.92,0:07:29.63,Default,,0,0,0,,that would mean I've\Nlost my son before I die.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.10,0:07:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you familiar at all with who\Nthe family of the other son is?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.76,0:07:40.76,Default,,0,0,0,,The other twins' family live in a\Nbig mansion in the next town over.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.82,0:07:43.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Poochie is the family's last name.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.54,0:07:48.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I, like, really don't get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.26,0:07:51.26,Default,,0,0,0,,What exactly do you see in that\Njuice delivery boy, anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.34,0:07:52.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.36,0:07:53.65,Default,,0,0,0,,But that butt, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.78,0:07:55.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Just stop it already.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.34,0:07:57.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I bet the loser comes from a poor family.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.74,0:07:59.48,Default,,0,0,0,,He probably doesn't\Neven go to high school.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.56,0:08:01.27,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why he delivers juice.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.42,0:08:03.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Perla!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.50,0:08:04.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Doesn't that bag belong to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.74,0:08:05.57,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.65,0:08:06.48,Default,,0,0,0,,That guy just took it!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.80,0:08:08.24,Default,,0,0,0,,He's a purse snatcher!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.54,0:08:10.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone catch that guy!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.72,0:08:21.90,Default,,0,0,0,,God damn it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.22,0:08:24.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I ended up breaking\Nout the store's window.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.24,0:08:27.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Totally gonna get fired from this job.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.58,0:08:30.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Plus, I'm not even allowed\Nto work under school policy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.38,0:08:34.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather Forecast's real\Nname is Wes Aquamarine.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.92,0:08:36.74,Default,,0,0,0,,He was 16 at the time,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.00,0:08:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,as innocent as anyone can be, and he had\Na strong belief in the idea of justice.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.66,0:08:44.52,Default,,0,0,0,,So, uh, thanks a bunch.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.02,0:08:46.86,Default,,0,0,0,,You saved my purse back there.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.98,0:08:51.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry, I'll tell them he's\Nthe one who broke the window.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.84,0:08:52.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Real?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.36,0:08:54.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.30,0:08:55.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Now you should go.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.12,0:09:02.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Um, my name's Wes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.58,0:09:04.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Some people call me Weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.18,0:09:05.54,Default,,0,0,0,,You wanna hang?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.40,0:09:14.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Two months had passed since the dying\Nmother's life-changing confession,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.56,0:09:16.85,Default,,0,0,0,,and Enrico was in utter mental turmoil.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.58,0:09:19.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Although he hadn't become a priest yet,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.98,0:09:22.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Enrico was still bound\Nby the seal of confession
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.40,0:09:24.96,Default,,0,0,0,,and could not disclose anything to anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.70,0:09:28.34,Default,,0,0,0,,He had to keep it a secret at all costs.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.74,0:09:33.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Otherwise, in the eyes of the church,\Nhe would be a failure as a man of God.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.18,0:09:39.12,Default,,0,0,0,,That mother will die soon, and she's going\Nto take her secret with her to the grave.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.38,0:09:42.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if I could convince\Nher to confess to everyone,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.28,0:09:46.30,Default,,0,0,0,,would we, or at the very\Nleast, would my brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.14,0:09:51.43,Default,,0,0,0,,be able to continue living as a real\Nfamily even after knowing the truth?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.60,0:09:53.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm back.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.18,0:09:55.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Welcome home.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.32,0:09:57.20,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.54,0:09:58.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like you're spacing out.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.04,0:10:01.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Did something happen to you at school?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.74,0:10:04.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Promise me, big bro.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.62,0:10:07.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm begging you not to tell Mama and Papa!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.08,0:10:10.46,Default,,0,0,0,,My grades have sort of tanked recently.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.86,0:10:13.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll catch up eventually,\Nbut what'll I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.08,0:10:17.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a boyfriend.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.44,0:10:18.58,Default,,0,0,0,,He's amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.44,0:10:22.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I met him two weeks ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.54,0:10:23.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I really like him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.82,0:10:25.68,Default,,0,0,0,,It's like our hearts are connected.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.76,0:10:27.50,Default,,0,0,0,,He's my soulmate.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.26,0:10:30.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Good for you, Perla.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.74,0:10:33.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks, big bro.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.96,0:10:37.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's start with the conclusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.46,0:10:40.64,Default,,0,0,0,,The soon-to-be priest Enrico\Nnever once uttered a word to his
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.72,0:10:44.84,Default,,0,0,0,,sister about her new boyfriend Weather\Nbeing his younger twin brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.48,0:10:50.02,Default,,0,0,0,,From here on out in the story,\NI would like you, the viewer,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.32,0:10:52.32,Default,,0,0,0,,to be the judge in deciding who is
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.74,0:10:54.66,Default,,0,0,0,,the one who has committed a sin.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.74,0:10:58.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Was it the mother who had sinned\Nfor having switched the babies?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.52,0:11:01.80,Default,,0,0,0,,The parents? Enrico?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.88,0:11:04.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Or was it Weather who didn't know a thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.48,0:11:07.08,Default,,0,0,0,,He looked into who\NWeather was to learn who
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.16,0:11:09.52,Default,,0,0,0,,it is that his sister\Nhad fallen in love with.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.60,0:11:14.76,Default,,0,0,0,,After discovering the shocking truth In\NEnrico's mind, there was only one solution.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.92,0:11:20.74,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter what the sacrifice, I have to\Nstop Perla from getting hurt in any way!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.30,0:11:24.92,Default,,0,0,0,,You look familiar, boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.10,0:11:27.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Ain't you the rich kid\Nwho goes to a seminary?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.74,0:11:30.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you sure you want to be doing this?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.18,0:11:32.90,Default,,0,0,0,,If everything goes well,\NI will double your pay.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.98,0:11:35.44,Default,,0,0,0,,There are only two\Nthings I want you to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.52,0:11:37.40,Default,,0,0,0,,First, do not ask any questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.02,0:11:40.14,Default,,0,0,0,,And second, make these two break up.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.22,0:11:45.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I bet if I make a couple of thugs threaten\NWes, he'll break things off with Perla.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.86,0:11:46.74,Default,,0,0,0,,That is all.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.06,0:11:49.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The only thing Perla\Nwill suffer from is an
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.12,0:11:51.74,Default,,0,0,0,,ordinary heartbreak that\Nanyone would experience.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.82,0:11:55.11,Default,,0,0,0,,The scars that will be left\Non her heart won't be fatal.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.82,0:11:56.65,Default,,0,0,0,,However,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.73,0:11:59.21,Default,,0,0,0,,what Enrico failed to\Nrealize was the true nature
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.30,0:12:02.12,Default,,0,0,0,,of this private detective\Nwho he sought to hire.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.34,0:12:05.20,Default,,0,0,0,,This man who has a proclivity\Nfor prying into secrets.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.28,0:12:08.04,Default,,0,0,0,,A man who holds a prejudice\Ndeep within his heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.12,0:12:10.24,Default,,0,0,0,,One which stemmed from the inhumane laws
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.32,0:12:12.74,Default,,0,0,0,,that dominated the South\Njust a century ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.82,0:12:15.29,Default,,0,0,0,,A prejudice that is very much still alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.12,0:12:20.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddamn sumbitch.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.36,0:12:25.08,Default,,0,0,0,,After doing some research on that West\Nkid, I discovered that back in 1972,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.52,0:12:29.88,Default,,0,0,0,,his whore mother married a black man,\Nall the while living in this very city.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.96,0:12:33.56,Default,,0,0,0,,So even though he looks white,\Nthat boy is a black man's son.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.64,0:12:37.62,Default,,0,0,0,,After this revelation, the P .I.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.70,0:12:39.23,Default,,0,0,0,,rallied his clan together.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.40,0:12:53.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry that pretty\Nlittle head, sweetheart.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.94,0:12:56.18,Default,,0,0,0,,We're gonna be punishing him, not you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.32,0:12:57.30,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right, baby.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.38,0:12:59.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Come here and give me\Na kiss, why don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.30,0:13:02.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Plant one on this nice\Nupstanding sheriff now, you hear?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.30,0:13:05.30,Default,,0,0,0,,You think you're all proper,\Ndon't you little slut?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.38,0:13:08.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Lucky for you, you're a white girl, so\Nit don't matter who you fool around with.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.00,0:13:10.24,Default,,0,0,0,,But not that shit, Stone!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.32,0:13:15.26,Default,,0,0,0,,An animal like him can't be allowed to taste\Nthose sweet lips of yours for a second!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.48,0:13:21.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Your older brother's the\None who asked me to do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.62,0:13:25.94,Default,,0,0,0,,And just so your ass is well aware, we've\Nalready paid a visit to your mama's house!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.02,0:13:29.46,Default,,0,0,0,,So you know, your childhood\Nhome is already up in flames!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.44,0:13:46.40,Default,,0,0,0,,In the end, who was the one truly\Nbeing punished in all of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.76,0:13:48.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Was it Weather? Perla?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.76,0:13:54.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps all anyone did up until this point\Nwas love someone with all their heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.32,0:14:00.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The only truth that can be found is that\Nlove brought about the worst-case scenario.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.30,0:14:03.22,Default,,0,0,0,,As for weather,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.54,0:14:08.26,Default,,0,0,0,,he was hung from a tree overlooking the\Ncliffside, and was left there to rot.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.88,0:14:11.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Until this day, Perla was pure of heart,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.60,0:14:16.04,Default,,0,0,0,,but the gentle breeze that once blew\Nthrough her heart swiftly came to an end.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.12,0:14:18.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Her love was like a spring sunshine.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.30,0:14:20.13,Default,,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.88,0:14:27.54,Default,,0,0,0,,My heart will no longer\Nfeel a thing anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.04,0:14:31.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Not even while standing\Nin the rain. Nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.98,0:14:37.80,Default,,0,0,0,,After uttering those words, Perla threw\Nherself off the cliff into the lake below,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.08,0:14:39.30,Default,,0,0,0,,taking her own life,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.54,0:14:43.54,Default,,0,0,0,,not knowing that her dearly beloved\Nweather still had a faint pulse.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.30,0:14:56.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Why in God's name? Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.66,0:14:58.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did it have to end like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.40,0:15:03.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did I even want to become\Na priest in the first place?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.18,0:15:05.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Why does fate bring two people together?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.00,0:15:09.90,Default,,0,0,0,,If they hadn't met, none of\Nthis would have ever happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.98,0:15:12.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop right there!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.76,0:15:18.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm telling you to stop that right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.96,0:15:21.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you dare cross your\Nheart in front of my sister!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.48,0:15:27.12,Default,,0,0,0,,While I'm here, damn it all!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.20,0:15:29.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Please don't let this be the end!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.28,0:15:30.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't take your life away!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.98,0:15:32.90,Default,,0,0,0,,None of this was perilous! Fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.98,0:15:34.84,Default,,0,0,0,,All she did was fall in love!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.92,0:15:36.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I will do anything that you ask of me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.96,0:15:38.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Just please bring her back!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.74,0:15:42.26,Default,,0,0,0,,If anyone should be damned\Nfor this, then it's me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.34,0:15:45.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you believe in gravity\Nbetween individuals?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.96,0:15:49.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you believe that fate brought\Nus together for a reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.26,0:15:52.80,Default,,0,0,0,,If you wish to see me again,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.34,0:15:54.52,Default,,0,0,0,,come and find me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.60,0:15:56.86,Default,,0,0,0,,That was him!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.94,0:15:59.38,Default,,0,0,0,,It was the voice of that strange man!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.46,0:16:01.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to see him!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.18,0:16:02.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I've forgotten when!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.62,0:16:05.74,Default,,0,0,0,,But he's the man who healed my\Nfoot back in the charnel house!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.82,0:16:08.76,Default,,0,0,0,,How could I have forgotten about?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.54,0:16:12.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Adam, until now, I just know\Nthat he gave me something.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.12,0:16:14.88,Default,,0,0,0,,An arrowhead, if I recall.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.36,0:16:23.48,Default,,0,0,0,,What? What?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.72,0:16:24.88,Default,,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.26,0:16:28.97,Default,,0,0,0,,The arrow that I've been\Nkeeping in my pocket?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.22,0:16:33.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Once a life has been taken away,\Nit can never fully be given back.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.92,0:16:38.32,Default,,0,0,0,,But if your desire is strong enough,\Nand it's what you truly wish for,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.76,0:16:41.88,Default,,0,0,0,,You will be capable of\Npreserving her memory forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.14,0:16:44.20,Default,,0,0,0,,The memory that lives in her heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.84,0:16:47.48,Default,,0,0,0,,This, my new friend, is your awakening.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.28,0:17:00.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, who the hell is there?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.20,0:17:04.78,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not that dumbass who asked me to\Ncheck if your wife's been cheating, are ya?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.86,0:17:06.42,Default,,0,0,0,,If you don't want to get pumped with lead,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.50,0:17:08.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I suggest you show that\Nugly Mega you are...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.50,0:17:09.33,Default,,0,0,0,,YAH!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.76,0:17:10.72,Default,,0,0,0,,What the fuck?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.88,0:17:14.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, you're big on information, yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.90,0:17:16.90,Default,,0,0,0,,If you know so much, then tell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.44,0:17:20.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Why the hell is an infestation\Nof snails coming out of your arm?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.98,0:17:23.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Where do all these\Nsnails keep coming from?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.84,0:17:25.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Why is it only happening around me?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.48,0:17:28.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, who the fuck are you, God?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.80,0:17:31.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it true that Perla's brother\Nis the one who hired you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.60,0:17:32.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't lie to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.54,0:17:34.56,Default,,0,0,0,,No, that can't be! How are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.50,0:17:40.38,Default,,0,0,0,,What's up with all these snails?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.60,0:17:42.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Why does this keep happening?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.68,0:17:48.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.74,0:17:50.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I really can't die.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.66,0:17:56.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Only when I try to use the gun,\Nthe chamber's filled with water.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.80,0:17:59.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Why is it that I'm still alive?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.80,0:18:03.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather was filled with an immense rage.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.58,0:18:07.70,Default,,0,0,0,,He was mad at the world for having\Nto deal with everything around him.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.86,0:18:09.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Angry that he was still alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.90,0:18:14.12,Default,,0,0,0,,And furious at himself for feeling\Nresponsible for Perla's death.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.50,0:18:17.56,Default,,0,0,0,,After realizing what happened to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.64,0:18:20.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather jumped off the cliff,\Ntrying to follow her lead.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.84,0:18:24.18,Default,,0,0,0,,But a sudden gust of\Nwind blew him back up.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.88,0:18:28.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Then he tried to drown\Nhimself in the lake.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.54,0:18:32.13,Default,,0,0,0,,But the strong waves would only\Npush him back onto the shore.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.58,0:18:34.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.49,0:18:36.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Why can't I just die and be with Perla?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.16,0:18:46.82,Default,,0,0,0,,In his despair, his rage\Nbecame a devastating fury.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.14,0:18:50.34,Default,,0,0,0,,His hatred started to extend\Nnot only to the townspeople,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.42,0:18:52.02,Default,,0,0,0,,but to humanity in general.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.02,0:18:59.48,Default,,0,0,0,,On the fourth night, a major snail\Ninfestation had invaded the town.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.80,0:19:01.52,Default,,0,0,0,,But why was it snails?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.76,0:19:03.94,Default,,0,0,0,,And where exactly did they come from?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.48,0:19:07.42,Default,,0,0,0,,No one was able to explain\Nthis sudden occurrence.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.26,0:19:12.02,Default,,0,0,0,,The only person who understood\Nwhat was going on was Enrico,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.30,0:19:13.96,Default,,0,0,0,,who woke up in a hospital.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.60,0:19:16.44,Default,,0,0,0,,It's Wes.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.82,0:19:18.04,Default,,0,0,0,,No, it's Weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.52,0:19:19.66,Default,,0,0,0,,My brother isn't dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.74,0:19:21.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Since he and I share the same blood,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.14,0:19:24.98,Default,,0,0,0,,the awakening of my powers\Nmust have awakened his own.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.06,0:19:28.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Just like how I wished for\Nthe preservation of memories,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.20,0:19:30.92,Default,,0,0,0,,this must be what Weather\Ndesired unconsciously.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.00,0:19:35.04,Default,,0,0,0,,If these snails were to start crawling\Nup my arm in order to do away with me,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.12,0:19:37.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I would have to finish off my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.60,0:19:43.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm willing to do anything from now\Non, even if that means I have to kill.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.34,0:19:48.74,Default,,0,0,0,,After I'm through with taking care\Nof weather, I shall go see that man.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.12,0:19:50.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The one who was named Dio.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.62,0:19:53.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Why does fate bring two people together?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.24,0:19:56.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I am convinced that he knows the answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.44,0:19:58.82,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what I want to learn.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.90,0:20:03.38,Default,,0,0,0,,The answer to that question is indeed the\Nstrongest power this world may ever know.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.46,0:20:04.94,Default,,0,0,0,,And the ultimate truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.32,0:20:10.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you happy?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.00,0:20:14.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Your sister Perla ended up dying\Nbecause of your fucking request.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.22,0:20:18.20,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, my fury isn't satisfied.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.64,0:20:20.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll make you pay right here and now.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.30,0:20:22.22,Default,,0,0,0,,You're wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.58,0:20:25.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I put this into motion\Nbecause I am your brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.08,0:20:29.38,Default,,0,0,0,,But that connection ends here today.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.46,0:20:31.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather, I'm going to eliminate you!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.52,0:20:41.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Weather, you are\Nmerely a hindrance to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.00,0:20:45.06,Default,,0,0,0,,So I shall banish you\Nalong with the Rainbow.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.88,0:20:49.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Like Perla, every one of\Nyour memories will vanish.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.96,0:20:53.62,Default,,0,0,0,,And those without any memories\Nleft are as good as dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.18,0:20:57.80,Default,,0,0,0,,You shall live out the rest of\Nyour days like a caged animal.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.54,0:21:09.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Prisoner number MA152403\Nhas been locked up!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.96,0:21:15.26,Default,,0,0,0,,My only reason for\Ncontinuing to live is to
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.34,0:21:17.87,Default,,0,0,0,,settle the score with\Nhim once and for all.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.30,0:21:20.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you saying they've come back to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.86,0:21:22.74,Default,,0,0,0,,You can remember everything now?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.06,0:21:24.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Then what are we doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.80,0:21:27.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Shouldn't we be heading to\Nwhere Jolene is right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.40,0:21:29.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I only came with you for Jolene!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.58,0:21:31.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't give a damn about your past!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.42,0:21:33.96,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't want to go\Nwhere Jolene is currently.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.04,0:21:35.51,Default,,0,0,0,,It would just be useless.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.62,0:21:39.28,Default,,0,0,0,,And anyway, I need you by\Nmy side so you can kill me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.46,0:21:42.22,Default,,0,0,0,,You have to take my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.42,0:21:45.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Anastasia, I beg you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.64,0:21:48.52,Default,,0,0,0,,And it's because of\Nthis gruesome method of
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.60,0:21:51.54,Default,,0,0,0,,eating that these bugs are\Nknown as snail suckers!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.58,0:21:53.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Aurora!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.70,0:21:57.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone, get in!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.68,0:22:01.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The suckers are crawling\Nin through the cracks!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.04,0:22:03.56,Default,,0,0,0,,What should we do, Jolene?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.64,0:22:06.46,Default,,0,0,0,,It doesn't matter if they're\Nin or out of the car.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.54,0:22:10.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Either way it goes, they're\Ngonna find us and start eating.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.32,0:22:13.44,Default,,0,0,0,,So while they're snacking,\Nwe're going after weather!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.28,0:22:30.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Although you think I cope,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.14,0:22:35.76,Default,,0,0,0,,my head is filled with hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.54,0:22:40.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Of some place
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.24,0:22:43.78,Default,,0,0,0,,other than here.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.50,0:22:50.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Although you think I smile.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.74,0:22:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Inside and all the while.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.02,0:22:59.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm wondering.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.68,0:23:03.36,Default,,0,0,0,,About my destiny.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.96,0:23:09.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm thinking about.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.68,0:23:18.08,Default,,0,0,0,,All the things I'd
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.16,0:23:24.50,Default,,0,0,0,,like to do in my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.42,0:23:29.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm a dreamer.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.40,0:23:34.14,Default,,0,0,0,,A distant dreamer.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.34,0:23:39.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Dreaming far away.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.72,0:23:44.52,Default,,0,0,0,,From today.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.14,0:24:04.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:38.68,0:24:39.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
